Feature: Update volume paths in pyspark_script.py using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx

  The pyspark_script.py must be updated so that only the volume paths for the three CSV files are replaced with their corresponding new paths as specified in volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx. All other logic and code structure must remain unchanged.

  Background:
    Given the file pyspark_script.py exists in the codebase
    And the file volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx exists with the following mappings:
      | old_volume_path                                                                 | new_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv      |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv     | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv            |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv             | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv                       |

  Scenario: Happy path - All volume paths are updated correctly
    Given pyspark_script.py contains the following volume paths:
      | path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv     |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv           |
    When the update logic is executed to replace old volume paths with new volume paths using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    Then pyspark_script.py should contain the following updated volume paths:
      | path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv      |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv      |
    And no other code or logic in pyspark_script.py should be changed

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - Old volume path not found in script
    Given pyspark_script.py does not contain the old volume path "<old_volume_path>"
    When the update logic is executed to replace old volume paths with new volume paths using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    Then the update process should log an error message "Old volume path <old_volume_path> not found in pyspark_script.py"
    And pyspark_script.py should remain unchanged

    Examples:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv               |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv             |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                     |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - Mapping sheet missing required mapping
    Given volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx does not contain a mapping for old volume path "<old_volume_path>"
    When the update logic is executed to replace old volume paths with new volume paths using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    Then the update process should log an error message "Mapping for old volume path <old_volume_path> not found in volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx"
    And pyspark_script.py should remain unchanged

    Examples:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv               |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv             |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                     |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Only volume paths are changed, other logic remains unchanged
    Given pyspark_script.py contains the old volume path "<old_volume_path>" and other code logic
    When the update logic is executed to replace old volume paths with new volume paths using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    Then only the volume path "<old_volume_path>" should be replaced with "<new_volume_path>"
    And all other code, variable names, and logic in pyspark_script.py should remain unchanged

    Examples:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   | new_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv               | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv      |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv             | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                     | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv      |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Volume path format and value
    Given the new volume path "<new_volume_path>" from volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    When the update logic is executed
    Then the new volume path in pyspark_script.py should match the format "/Volumes/<catalog>/<schema>/<subfolder>/<filename>.csv"
    And the filename should be one of:
      | 19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv           |
      | 19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv|
      | 19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv           |

    Examples:
      | new_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv      |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv      |

  Scenario: Error scenario - Mapping sheet is missing or unreadable
    Given volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx is missing or cannot be read
    When the update logic is executed
    Then the update process should log an error message "volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx is missing or unreadable"
    And pyspark_script.py should remain unchanged

  Scenario: Error scenario - New volume path is invalid format
    Given volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains a new_volume_path with invalid format "invalid_path"
    When the update logic is executed
    Then the update process should log an error message "New volume path invalid_path is not a valid path format"
    And pyspark_script.py should remain unchanged

  Scenario: Acceptance criteria - Final output code validation
    Given the update logic has been executed successfully
    When reviewing the final pyspark_script.py
    Then the only changes present should be the updated volume paths as per volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    And all other code, comments, and logic should remain exactly as before

